    </div>
    </li> <li> <para-num num="[0176]"> </para-num> <div id="p-0191" num="0176" class="description-line">It is understood from Table 4 that Examples 11 and 12 are excellent in charging and discharging characteristics as compared to Example 13. It is understood from the above that, when aromatic polyamide is used as the heat resistant resin, the end group concentration ratio of the aromatic polyamide is preferably [COOX]/[NH<sub>2</sub>]≧1. While Example 13 is slightly inferior in cycle characteristics, it suffers no problem in practical use, but has heat resistance, shutdown characteristics, flame retardancy and handling property that are equivalent to Example 1, thereby attaining sufficiently the objects of the invention.</div>
    </li> <heading id="h-0054">INDUSTRIAL APPLICABILITY</heading>
    <li> <para-num num="[0177]"> </para-num> <div id="p-0192" num="0177" class="description-line">The invention is effectively utilized as techniques for enhancing characteristics of a nonaqueous secondary battery.</div>
    
  </li> </ul>
  </div>
  </section>

  <section itemprop="claims" itemscope>
    <h2>Claims (<span itemprop="count">17</span>)</h2>
    
    <div itemprop="content" html><div mxw-id="PCLM38327887" lang="EN" load-source="patent-office" class="claims">
    <div class="claim"> <div id="CLM-00001" num="00001" class="claim">
      <div class="claim-text"> <b>1</b>. A separator for a nonaqueous secondary battery comprising a polyolefin microporous membrane at least one surface of which is laminated with a heat resistant porous layer containing a heat resistant resin,
<div class="claim-text">the heat resistant porous layer containing an inorganic filler containing a metallic hydroxide that undergoes dehydration reaction at a temperature of 200 to 400° C.,</div> <div class="claim-text">wherein the heat resistant resin is meta-type wholly aromatic polyamide.</div> </div>
    </div>
    </div> <div class="claim-dependent"> <div id="CLM-00002" num="00002" class="claim">
      <div class="claim-text"> <b>2</b>. The separator for a nonaqueous secondary battery according to <claim-ref idref="CLM-00001">claim 1</claim-ref>, characterized in that the heat resistant resin has a molecular weight distribution Mw/Mn of 5≦Mw/Mn≦100 and a weight average molecular weight of 8.0×10<sup>3 </sup>to 1.0×10<sup>6</sup>.</div>
    </div>
    </div> <div class="claim-dependent"> <div id="CLM-00003" num="00003" class="claim">
      <div class="claim-text"> <b>3</b>. The separator for a nonaqueous secondary battery according to <claim-ref idref="CLM-00001">claim 1</claim-ref>, characterized in that the heat resistant resin contains a low molecular weight polymer having a molecular weight of 8,000 or less in an amount of 1 to 15% by weight.</div>
    </div>
    </div> <div class="claim-dependent"> <div id="CLM-00004" num="00004" class="claim">
      <div class="claim-text"> <b>4</b>. The separator for a nonaqueous secondary battery according to <claim-ref idref="CLM-00001">claim 1</claim-ref>, characterized in that the heat resistant resin is wholly aromatic polyamide, and the wholly aromatic polyamide has an end group concentration ratio of [COOX]/[NH<sub>2</sub>]≧1 (wherein X represents an alkali metal or an alkaline earth metal).</div>
    </div>
    </div> <div class="claim"> <div id="CLM-00005" num="00005" class="claim">
      <div class="claim-text"> <b>5</b>. A separator for a nonaqueous secondary battery comprising a polyolefin microporous membrane at least one surface of which is laminated with a heat resistant porous layer containing a heat resistant resin,
<div class="claim-text">the heat resistant porous layer containing an inorganic filler containing a metallic hydroxide that undergoes dehydration reaction at a temperature of 200 to 400° C.,</div> <div class="claim-text">wherein the heat resistant porous layer has a porosity of 60 to 90%.</div> </div>
    </div>
    </div> <div class="claim"> <div id="CLM-00006" num="00006" class="claim">
      <div class="claim-text"> <b>6</b>. A separator for a nonaqueous secondary battery comprising a polyolefin microporous membrane at least one surface of which is laminated with a heat resistant porous layer containing a heat resistant resin,
<div class="claim-text">the heat resistant porous layer containing an inorganic filler containing a metallic hydroxide that undergoes dehydration reaction at a temperature of 200 to 400° C.,</div> <div class="claim-text">wherein a coated amount of the heat resistant porous layer is 2 to 10 g/m<sup>2</sup>.</div> </div>
    </div>
    </div> <div class="claim"> <div id="CLM-00007" num="00007" class="claim">
      <div class="claim-text"> <b>7</b>. A separator for a nonaqueous secondary battery comprising a polyolefin microporous membrane at least one surface of which is laminated with a heat resistant porous layer containing a heat resistant resin,
<div class="claim-text">the heat resistant porous layer containing an inorganic filler containing a metallic hydroxide that undergoes dehydration reaction at a temperature of 200 to 400° C.,</div> <div class="claim-text">wherein the separator has an air permeability (JIS P8117) of 500 sec/100 cc or less.</div> </div>
    </div>
    </div> <div class="claim"> <div id="CLM-00008" num="00008" class="claim">
      <div class="claim-text"> <b>8</b>. A separator for a nonaqueous secondary battery comprising a polyolefin microporous membrane at least one surface of which is laminated with a heat resistant porous layer containing a heat resistant resin,
<div class="claim-text">the heat resistant porous layer containing an inorganic filler containing a metallic hydroxide that undergoes dehydration reaction at a temperature of 200 to 400° C.,</div> <div class="claim-text">wherein the separator has a membrane resistance of 0.5 to 10 ohm·cm<sup>2</sup>.</div> </div>
    </div>
    </div> <div class="claim"> <div id="CLM-00009" num="00009" class="claim">
      <div class="claim-text"> <b>9</b>. A separator for a nonaqueous secondary battery comprising a polyolefin microporous membrane at least one surface of which is laminated with a heat resistant porous layer containing a heat resistant resin,
<div class="claim-text">the heat resistant porous layer containing an inorganic filler containing a metallic hydroxide that undergoes dehydration reaction at a temperature of 200 to 400° C.,</div> <div class="claim-text">wherein the separator has a heat contraction ratio at 175° C. of 30% or less in both MD and TD.</div> </div>
    </div>
    </div> <div class="claim"> <div id="CLM-00010" num="00010" class="claim">
      <div class="claim-text"> <b>10</b>. A separator for a nonaqueous secondary battery comprising a polyolefin microporous membrane at least one surface of which is laminated with a heat resistant porous layer containing a heat resistant resin,
<div class="claim-text">the heat resistant porous layer containing an inorganic filler containing a metallic hydroxide that undergoes dehydration reaction at a temperature of 200 to 400° C.,</div> <div class="claim-text">wherein the inorganic filler is surface-treated with a silane coupling agent.</div> </div>
    </div>
    </div> <div class="claim-dependent"> <div id="CLM-00011" num="00011" class="claim">
      <div class="claim-text"> <b>11</b>. The separator for a nonaqueous secondary battery according to <claim-ref idref="CLM-00001">claim 1</claim-ref>, characterized in that the metallic hydroxide is at least one of aluminum hydroxide and magnesium hydroxide.</div>
    </div>
    </div> <div class="claim-dependent"> <div id="CLM-00012" num="00012" class="claim">
      <div class="claim-text"> <b>12</b>. The separator for a nonaqueous secondary battery according to <claim-ref idref="CLM-00001">claim 1</claim-ref>, characterized in that the inorganic filler has an average particle diameter of 0.1 to 1 μm.</div>
    </div>
    </div> <div class="claim-dependent"> <div id="CLM-00013" num="00013" class="claim">
      <div class="claim-text"> <b>13</b>. The separator for a nonaqueous secondary battery according to <claim-ref idref="CLM-00001">claim 1</claim-ref>, characterized in that the heat resistant porous layer contains the inorganic filler in an amount of 50 to 95% by weight.</div>
    </div>
    </div> <div class="claim-dependent"> <div id="CLM-00014" num="00014" class="claim">
      <div class="claim-text"> <b>14</b>. The separator for a nonaqueous secondary battery according to <claim-ref idref="CLM-00005">claim 5</claim-ref>, characterized in that the heat resistant resin is at least one of wholly aromatic polyamide, polyimide, polyamideimide, polysulfone, polyketone, polyetherketone, polyetherimide and cellulose.</div>
    </div>
    </div> <div class="claim-dependent"> <div id="CLM-00015" num="00015" class="claim">
      <div class="claim-text"> <b>15</b>. The separator for a nonaqueous secondary battery according to <claim-ref idref="CLM-00001">claim 1</claim-ref>, characterized in that the separator for a nonaqueous secondary battery has a thickness of 25 μm or less, the polyolefin microporous membrane has a thickness of 5 μm or more, and the heat resistant porous layer has a thickness of 2 μm or more.</div>
    </div>
    </div> <div class="claim-dependent"> <div id="CLM-00016" num="00016" class="claim">
      <div class="claim-text"> <b>16</b>. The separator for a nonaqueous secondary battery according to <claim-ref idref="CLM-00001">claim 1</claim-ref>, characterized in that the heat resistant porous layer is coated on both surfaces of the polyethylene microporous membrane.</div>
    </div>
    </div> <div class="claim-dependent"> <div id="CLM-00017" num="00017" class="claim">
      <div class="claim-text"> <b>17</b>. A nonaqueous secondary battery comprising a positive electrode, a negative electrode, a separator provided between the electrodes, and a nonaqueous electrolytic solution,
<div class="claim-text">characterized in that the separator is the separator for a nonaqueous secondary battery according to <claim-ref idref="CLM-00001">claim 1</claim-ref>.</div> </div>
    </div>
  </div> </div>
  </div>
  </section>

